From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 13:26:20 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] logging: preserve explicit float precision in deferred
 messages

Support FLOAT message placeholders :f/:g and :.Nf/:.Ng, bounded to precision 0..18. Render on the consumer with the same tinyformat backend as original printf calls, while structured fields retain raw numeric values. Invalid formats remain literal and lint rejects them. Introduce the actual elapsed_ms FLOAT vocabulary key for forthcoming millisecond diagnostics. The earlier independent JSON encoder correction already maps nonfinite values to null.

Manually authored API implementation and fixtures, not a call conversion. No production callers converted here. Artifact-only original/modified event renderer control fails before and passes after: eight numeric values, 64 original printf comparisons and 24 unsupported-spec checks. Native API test compares full message text, finite raw JSON and null for nonfinite input; lint fixtures reject unsupported formats and non-FLOAT keys.

All five targets and logging_event_tests pass. Full standard functional gate: {'total': 320, 'failed': 0, 'errors': 0, 'skipped': 61, 'passed': 259}. Frozen tree 37a0ca6442990add21263cff42b66dbd7abf1e21. No extended suite.

Coordinator integration provenance (canonical283 to ordered301):
